a52sxq: QUP serial engines may name their wrapper with "qcom,wrapper-core" (5.4 DT layout)

Qualcomm's 6.12 drivers find the QUP wrapper of a serial engine as dev->parent only, so the SE
nodes must be children of the wrapper node and their devices live under
/sys/devices/platform/soc/9c0000.qcom,qupv3_0_geni_se/98c000.i2c/... On 5.4 the SE nodes are
direct /soc children with a qcom,wrapper-core phandle: /sys/devices/platform/soc/98c000.i2c/...
The Galaxy A52s ROM's SELinux genfscon labels (sysfs_battery for the SM5714 fuel gauge,
sysfs_power_writable for the touch "enabled" node, ...) are keyed to the 5.4 paths
(research/sepolicy/PATHS.md). geni_se_common_wrapper_dev() takes the phandle when present and
falls back to dev->parent, so both layouts work with these modules; the board tree is moved to
the 5.4 layout by drivers612/boarddt/tools/sysfscompat.py.

